Alembic migrations for PLIXOR.

The database URL is read from application settings (core.config.settings),
not from alembic.ini, so migrations and the app can never disagree about
which database they mean. Set DATABASE_URL in the environment before
running any command here.

Everyday use
------------

    alembic upgrade head            # apply everything outstanding
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "what changed"
    alembic downgrade -1            # step back one revision
    alembic current                 # what the database is at

Railway applies `alembic upgrade head` automatically via the Procfile's
release command.

ONE-TIME STEP for a database created before migrations existed
--------------------------------------------------------------

Until now the app built its schema by calling `Base.metadata.create_all()`
on startup. A database built that way already contains all 14 tables but has
no `alembic_version` row, so `alembic upgrade head` would try to CREATE TABLE
over tables that exist and fail.

Run this ONCE against each such database (production, staging, and any local
plixor.db you want to keep):

    alembic stamp head

That records the baseline revision as already applied without touching any
table. Afterwards `alembic upgrade head` behaves normally.

A brand-new, empty database needs no stamp -- run `alembic upgrade head`
directly.
